{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('state.json'))\ni=[x for x in st['interpretations'] if x['investigation_id'].startswith('f7da39e9771e40d29f8d7ec3d1c7d886')][-1]\nprint(i['id'], i['conclusion'], i['defect_claim'])\nprint('executions', json.dumps(i['executions']))\nprint()\nfor l in i.get('limitations',[]): print('*', l[:260])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"6dbbc1ce109a40be9ca9f10d75551f8d-interpretation-0 violated asserted\nexecutions {\"d436029b08c5425aa5aec577901cb8ba\": [1, 3], \"0726bba116ac415fa38b99b96a88290f\": [1, 3], \"4185f1615cf54e4fbd4801044480416d\": [1, 3]}\n\n* Both runs exercised one cluster size (four members, three voters after the demotion) and one relationship: a leader transferring to a non-leader member. Transfer initiated while the leader later regains leadership, and clusters whose only non-voter is the sole\n* Leaderless counts are sampled every ~10 ms over roughly 4.7 s of the 5 s window (470 samples); a gap shorter than the sample spacing would be missed, so 80 ms is a lower bound for the trigger and the control's zero does not prove uninterrupted leadership.\n* Only immediate convergence was observed: the demoted member's own view reported the new role within the first poll (0 ms), so no case exercised a target whose configuration still showed it as a voter at request time.\n* That the voter members had committed the demotion before the transfer is inferred from their rejection and term adoption, not from reading each voter's configuration.\n* Out of scope: whether an unprivileged or misconfigured peer could send TimeoutNow directly, even though timeoutNow performs no term, leader or membership check (raft.go:2232-2237); that path was not exercised here.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
